> My Dog turned Dragon killed the only priest in the game. Is there a way
> to repair armor, I dont want to take off my jumping boots or ESP helmet

Yes, you can repair armor but it's not worth it until the armor's
enchanted all the way up--read ?enchant armor while confused and it'll
repair instead of enchanting.  But you get better AC with those
helms/boots by enchanting them than by fixing them.  If you have
?destroy armor you can use them to rustproof things before they're
damaged, but that won't fix things that are already damaged.

I'll repeat, though, you should be able to get much lower AC by
scrounging things above you in the dungeon.  It's incredibly rare that
you don't find at least a couple +1/+2 items in the mines.  Almost
worst case (assuming there's at least 1 set of dwarvish mithril) would
be 6 for mithril, 4 for the starting shield, 1 for a cloak, 1 for
gloves = -2 AC.  But you should be able to find a few +1/+2 items.
Getting in the -5 or better range isn't unthinkable even without buying
protection, especially if there were a couple of barracks you've
unearthed already.

